                       of small firms. The final type of merger is based on a perception of a future
                       convergence of industries. Disney purchased ABC-TV and Radio, envisioning
                       a convergence of content and media channels. Often firms use an acquisition to
                       restore a sense of vitality to their businesses and, they hope, unleash a subse-
                       quent surge in performance [Vermeulen, 2005].
